          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_notions"} Related notions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Just as the notion of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiomatization
            of basic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category-theoretic
            properties of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} category of sets
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %em category with class structure
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %em category of classes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classes"} classes
          %p
            In contrast to the situation for elementary toposes, however, there is no unique such axiomatization with a privileged status in the literature; the field of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+set+theory"} algebraic set theory
            includes many variations. Here we describe the first such axiomatization due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#JM"} Joyal-Moerdijk
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We work in a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that is assumed to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+pretopos"} Heyting pretopos
            with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#JM"} Joyal-Moerdijk
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong class of open maps
              (with collection) in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              of morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              that satisfies the following properties:
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                contains all isomorphisms and is closed under compositions;
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is closed under
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+changes"} base changes
              %li
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\in S
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                along an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in S
              %li
                the canonical maps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to 1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\sqcup 1\to 1
                belong to
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is closed under binary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+morphisms"} category of morphisms
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %li
                if
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo =
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g=f\circ p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\in S
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in S
              %li
                (collection axiom) for any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon Y\to X
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to A
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in S
                there is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon B\to A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon Z\to B
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\in S
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo :
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w:Z\to Y
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mi g
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mi p
                      %mi w
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h g=f p w
                and the induced map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi A
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z\to B\times_A X
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            %p
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong class of small maps
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a class of open maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              such that every map in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponentiable
              and there is a universal map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi\colon E\to U
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with the following property: for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in S
              we can
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              along some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              such that the resulting morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              along some morphism in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              are known as
              = succeed "." do
                %strong small maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              %strong small
              if the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to 1
              is small.
          %p
            Intuitively, small maps are maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Y
            for which preimages of any element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are sets as opposed to proper classes.
          %p
            In any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+pretopos"} Heyting pretopos
            the class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponentiable maps
            satisfies all the axioms of a class of open maps with a possible exception of the collection axiom.
          %p
            The collection axiom can be reformulated by saying that the
            %em small powerset
            functor preserves
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is as the free
            = succeed "-complete" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suplattice"} suplattice
            generated by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A category with a class of small maps admits
              %strong powerclasses
              if for any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              there is an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P C
              with a small relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in\subset C\times P C
              such that any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and any small relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\subset C\times X
              there is a unique morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\colon X\to P C
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\to C\times X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in\to C\times P C
              along the map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi C
                      %mo ×
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_C \times r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P C
              must be small.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong universal class
              is an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              such that any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to C
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong category of classes
              or a
              %strong class category
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
              with a class of small maps that admits small powerclasses and a universal class.
          %p
            The full subcategory of small objects and small maps of any class category is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
